{"name":"Milk and Cookies","hex":"#e9e1df","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"milk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A white liquid produced by the mammary glands of female mammals to nourish their young. From certain animals, especially cows, it is also called dairy milk and is a common food for humans as a beverage or used to produce various dairy products such as butter, cheese, and yogurt.","A white (or whitish) liquid obtained from a vegetable source such as almonds, coconuts, oats, rice, or soy beans."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To express milk from (a mammal, especially a cow).","To draw (milk) from the breasts or udder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/milk"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.","Yet; but."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"cookies","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of cookie","plural of cooky"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of cookie"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cookies"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dunking (biscuit)","blocks":[{"text":"To dunk or to dip a biscuit or some other food, usually baked goods, means to partially submerge it into a drink - especially tea, coffee, or milk - before eating it. Dunking releases more flavour from confections by dissolving the sugars, while also softening their texture. Dunking can be used to melt chocolate on biscuits to create a richer flavour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg/330px-Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunking_(biscuit)"},{"title":"Milk","blocks":[{"text":"Milk is usually a white liquid food produced by the mammary glands of lactating mammals. It is the primary source of nutrition for young mammals before they are able to digest solid food. Milk contains many nutrients, including calcium and protein, as well as lactose and saturated fat; the enzyme lactase is needed to break down lactose. Immune factors and immune-modulating components in milk contribute to milk immunity. The first milk, which is called colostrum, contains antibodies and immune-modulating components that strengthen the immune system against many diseases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/330px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk"},{"title":"Cookie","blocks":[{"text":"A cookie is a sweet biscuit with high sugar and fat content. Cookie dough is softer than that used for other types of biscuit, and they are cooked longer at lower temperatures. The dough typically contains flour, sugar, egg, and some type of oil or fat. It may include other ingredients such as raisins, oats, chocolate chips, or nuts. Cookie texture varies from crisp and crunchy to soft and chewy, depending on the exact combination of ingredients and methods used to create them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg/330px-2ChocolateChipCookies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cookie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg/500px-Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg/500px-Dunking_a_biscuit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dunking a Lotus Biscoff biscuit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADunking_a_biscuit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Dunking_Oreo.jpg/500px-Dunking_Oreo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Dunking_Oreo.jpg/1280px-Dunking_Oreo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Dunking_Oreo.jpg/500px-Dunking_Oreo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Oreo cookie dunked into milk.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADunking_Oreo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/500px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/1280px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg/500px-Glass_of_Milk_%2833657535532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of cow milk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlass_of_Milk_(33657535532).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/500px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/1280px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Melkkarussell.jpg/500px-Melkkarussell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th